# K03 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09, -07 Q2; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:666, :668): a named Structure is
# visible throughout the unit both ways, so a head that names one is known before its tail is read, whatever the
# tail is written as.
# `Later: 3` above `Later:` is Later's application with 3 -- an ordinary named Structure takes no argument: refused
# at the line, never a second definition of Later.
Later: 3
Later:
    int: v 1
end: Later
fn: m () int
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
